 "hypothesis": "The official 19-band GeoDAWN stack carries a fault signature that generalises to faults absent from the public USGS/INGENIOUS catalogue; a per-cell classifier trained on the visible catalogue with catalogue-independent features recovers withheld fault segments.",
 "mechanism": "Quantile transforms of every magnetic, gravity, elevation, geodetic, conductivity and heat-flow band (global rank + 9-cell local contrast) feed a gradient-boosted classifier; the probability field is thinned to a candidate pool by non-maximum suppression and selected by the shared exact-DTI allocator; the mapped-catalogue band is excluded because the organiser masks known-fault pixels from scoring.",
 "named_non_fault_mimic": "lithologic and weathering contacts, buried basin-margin flexures, and mafic magnetic-source edges that mimic a fault's local magnetic/gravity contrast.",
